The correction was timestamped 19:15:00 UTC. The standards review ran at 19:18:27 UTC â€” after the correction was logged. The standards layer produced a `standards-cleared` finding named `attention-preserve-correction` with message "hidden correction state corrected," which indicates it detected the existence of a correction record but did not enforce the correction's `must_not_include` body constraint against the actual body text. The standards gate returned `publishable: true` despite the body violating the explicit `must_not_include` requirement. The root failure is in the correction-application step: the correction metadata was written but the body URLs were not updated before the manuscript moved forward.

